{% extends "layouts/catalog.html.jinja" %}
{% from "includes/block-example.html.jinja" import render_block_example %}
{% from "includes/code-snippet.html.jinja" import render_code_snippet %}
{% from "includes/documentation-reference.html.jinja" import render_reference with context %}
{% from "includes/page-header.html.jinja" import render_page_header with context %}
{% from "pages/blocks/previews/toc.html.jinja" import toc_demo with context %}

{% block title %}Table of Contents — Moo UI{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  {{ render_page_header("Table of Contents", "Navigate sections of a document with a list or a compact control that shows the current section.") }}

  <div class="moo-component-examples">
    {% set demo %}{{ toc_demo() }}{% endset %}
    {{ render_block_example(
      "toc-document", "Placement guide", "Explore one document at desktop, tablet and mobile widths.", demo,
      preview_class="moo-example__preview--shell",
      frame_src=site_href("blocks/previews/toc.html", root_path),
      frame_width=1280, frame_height=900,
      frame_viewports=[
        {"label": "Mobile", "icon": "smartphone", "width": 390, "height": 900},
        {"label": "Tablet", "icon": "tablet", "width": 768, "height": 900},
        {"label": "Desktop", "icon": "monitor", "width": 1280, "height": 900, "active": true}
      ],
      show_header=false
    ) }}

    <h2 id="usage" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">Usage</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">Supply ordered section IDs and plain-text labels. Moo UI renders native fragment links; the host owns headings, content and layout. Empty sections render nothing. A single section remains available.</p>
    <p class="mb-4">Use the viewport controls to resize the same live document. Choose a section or scroll inside the preview to follow its active indicator. The preview owns its URL fragments and scroll area independently from this documentation page.</p>

    <h2 id="responsive-placement" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">Responsive placement</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">The desktop list stays beside the article. Below <code>lg</code>, the compact presentation moves into the header above the scrolling content. Both use the same section data with unique navigation IDs and complementary Bootstrap visibility utilities.</p>
    <p class="mb-4">The compact menu spans its navigation row, wraps long labels and uses Bootstrap's Dropdown keyboard and dismissal behavior. Supporting blocks render once and follow the article when the columns stack. Translate the labels for each document; logical spacing follows its text direction.</p>

    <h2 id="runtime" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">Runtime and placement</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">Import <code>TableOfContents</code> from <code>@wpmoo/ui/toc.js</code> and initialize each supplied <code>[data-toc]</code> root. Use <code>refresh()</code> after replacing targets and <code>dispose()</code> when removing a view. The previous <code>@wpmoo/ui/table-of-contents.js</code> entrypoint remains a compatibility re-export of the same constructor.</p>
    {% set init_code %}
  import TableOfContents from "@wpmoo/ui/toc.js";

  const reader = document.getElementById("main-content");
  reader.classList.add("scroll-smooth");

  document.querySelectorAll("[data-toc]").forEach(element => {
    TableOfContents.getOrCreateInstance(element);
  });
    {% endset %}
    {{ render_code_snippet("toc-initialization", init_code, language="js") }}
    <p class="mt-4 mb-4">Importing the module alone does not initialize a document. For a JavaScript-disabled host, use the list.</p>
    <p class="mb-4"><code>content_id</code> limits resolution to an explicit content region inside the same Moo owner. <code>scroll_root_id</code> identifies the scrolling ancestor of that content. Omitted values use the nearest Moo owner and document scrolling. A missing scope leaves the native links available and skips tracking.</p>
    <p class="mb-4">The host owns fixed header geometry. With the App layout, place the compact navigation in the header above the scrolling main region, and supply that region's ID. For other layouts, a finite nonnegative <code>activationOffset</code> option sets the tracking line. The component does not change layout styles or override native scrolling.</p>
    <p class="mb-4">For animated native fragment navigation, apply the Core <code>scroll-smooth</code> utility to the actual scroll container inside its Moo owner. The utility uses <code>scroll-behavior</code> and switches to immediate scrolling when the visitor prefers reduced motion. Links retain their native URL fragments and browser history.</p>
    <p class="mb-4">Two presentations can share section data with unique IDs and complementary Bootstrap visibility utilities. Ordinary aside content renders once and can stack below the article on narrow screens.</p>

  </div>

  {{ render_reference("For the compact control's native behavior, see the", "https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/components/dropdowns/", "Bootstrap Dropdown documentation") }}
{% endblock %}
